 "task": "Descriptive comparison of the LivenessNet run with four subject folds and three training seeds (20261103-FOLDSRUN-e174812) and of N1 (20261024-N1-LivenessNet-fb93496) on the same 3,000 frames of the manifest nuaa_cnn_test, from the existing per-frame scores and the thresholds already frozen: per seed, the metrics of both experiments, their differences, a paired bootstrap over subjects, the paired decisions per frame and counts per subject. No training, no inference, no image read, no new threshold.",
 "declarations": {
  "descriptive": true,
  "post_hoc": true,
  "no_training": true,
  "no_inference": true,
  "no_images_read": true,
  "no_new_threshold": true,
  "training_roles": "The training roles differ: N1 was trained on 9 subjects (sessions 01-02 of the official train list), and 9 of the 16 subjects of the 3,000 frames are those training subjects, seen in other sessions; in the folds run every frame is scored by the model of the fold that held its subject out, so none of the 16 subjects was in the training of the model that scored it (fitting on the 8 subjects of two other folds with every session represented, dev on the 4 subjects of the next fold).",
  "auroc_four_models": "The AUROC of the folds run pools the scores of four different models (one per fold) on one ranking; it is not the AUROC of a single model.",
  "n1_threshold": "N1 has only the fixed threshold 0.5; the dev difference compares the folds run at its frozen dev thresholds with N1 at 0.5",
  "indicative": "Indicative: the 3,000 frames are the fixed spread sample of session 03 on which N1 was tested (the 300 frames of C1 are inside it), correlated within subject and capture; three seeds give a range, not a confidence interval; the bootstrap over 16 subjects is coarse, and subject-level ACER is defined only for subjects with both classes.",
  "no_causality": "No causal reading: the two experiments differ in training subjects, sessions, sample sizes, dev sets and thresholds at once; a difference is an association with the whole design, not with one factor.",
  "limits": "One dataset, one attack type (print); post hoc comparison after both runs, requested by the coordinator; no statistical test."
 },
 "decision": "attack if score_attack > threshold (tie = bona fide)",
